Round 44 is finished, committed and pushed (`d79cf39`). The frequency-match bias (option (a)) helps at rung 2 (the transformer model); it made no significant difference at rung 3 (the loop model). No rung has beaten the type-aware greedy baseline (E0+) on interposer (ip) boards yet. Everything was run on one seed only, so these results still need confirming.

**Finished this round**
- **r2a training** ended at 07:15 with no out-of-memory errors. It used the same budget as r2 and r3a: 0.77 h distillation plus 1.27 h RL, best checkpoint at iteration 300.
- **r2a 10×10 evaluation** (50 problems per board type), against r2 without the bias, with paired bootstrap 95% CIs:

| Board | Success-rate difference | Count ratio |
|---|---|---|
| pcb | +0.08 [+0.02, +0.16] | 1.003 |
| pkg | +0.12 [+0.02, +0.24] | 0.987 |
| ip | +0.00 | 1.011 |

  The pcb and pkg gains are the only architecture change so far whose CI excludes 0, while decap counts stay the same. One caveat: r2 had a low pkg success rate (0.72 against 0.88 for r3), so r2a may simply have caught up to the r3 level. More seeds will tell.
- **Against E0+ on ip**, r2a uses about the same number of decaps (count ratio 1.029, CI [1.000, 1.067]), so it does not beat that baseline. I recorded this as it is. On pcb and pkg it uses far fewer (0.20 and 0.58 of E0+), but E0+ is a weak baseline there because it can't mix decap types.
- The day-1 evaluation of r3 after distillation only also finished. RL raised r3's ip success rate from 0.82 to 0.98.

**Decisions (logged in `PROGRESS.md`)**
- I picked r2a as the provisional final candidate for the seed runs and added r2a seeds 1 and 2 to the end of the GPU queue. Nothing ahead of them was moved, so the prior-paper baselines and ladder seeds still run first.
- I'm holding off on building option (c), the multi-step draft check loop. The prior-paper baselines run first on the GPU, about 4 hours. This round I only wrote down that (c) needs to place several decaps ahead to be new; a design note goes in `PROPOSALS.md` next round.

**Running now**
- **GPU:** the Park-style baseline (bp_park) started at 07:15 with no out-of-memory errors. It should finish around 09:20, and its 10×10 evaluation then fills the prior-work section of `RESULTS.md`. The Manoharan-style baseline (bm_manoharan) trains next.
- **CPU:** the day-1 evaluation of r2 after distillation only, then the 16×16 E0+ runs, plus the separate 16×16 greedy+prune job.
- Pod memory is 26 GiB of 60, with no OOM kills.
